A||N||21||stimpy||How NOT to race an Integra.||||10||
Z||000000||stimpy||09-26-2001||12:34 PM||||Last night while driving around town I started getting the ol "fly by" from a 2nd generation Teggy. You know the kind, stock looking except for exhaust and wheels. The kind that always makes me nervous. (If they ain't spending it on stickers, wing and blue marker lights, the money must be going under the hood.) Well, as he got at my back bumper, I downshifted to third and kept with him for about 100', before traffic started coming onto the street. (Northwest Expressway, 6 lanes divided by wide median, 1 mile between lights. No kittens in sight) At that time he just kept pulling as I backed off. Up ahead though, I saw the light change to yellow, then red. Hehe, yer my beeatch now, I thought. Light turns green and I pull away quickly. At about 3500, it feels like I hit the rev limiter. Wha? So I shift to second, still ahead but the distance is closing. 3500 rpm again, bogs again. At this point I'm pretty convinced I'm killing something, and it ain't the Integra. I scan my guages, looking for low oil pressure, low voltage, nope. Oh, I get it! My gas guage is on the interesting side of empty! Ooops! I nurse it to the closest gas station and luckily make it to the pump without running dry.<P>Next time, silver Integra boy!<BR> <BR><P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif">   <BR>My Fiero website-&gt; <A HREF="http://www.dancinghamsters.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.dancinghamsters.com/</A>||||reg||10
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||09-26-2001||12:44 PM||||LMAO!!! Gotta hate it when that happens.  <P>My Dad's famous words of wisdom... first: It'll make it.  followed by: it still shows an 1/8th of the tank... gauge must be off somehow.<P>And I'll have to admit- I've had the GT coughing and wheezing around corners.  Even had it die one time as I was rolling up to the pump.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||10
Z||000002||Raydar||09-26-2001||01:21 PM||||"Interesting side of empty?" LOL<P>Glad you didn't have to take the shoe-leather express. Sucks when that happens.<BR>I've never run any of my Fieros out of gas. Made a "dead stick" landing in a gas station with a Ford F-100 a few years ago, though.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||onfire||09-26-2001||02:04 PM||||What's really cool is when it says you have a quarter of a tank left. Then it runs out of gas on the freeway. Luckily it was only a block to the gas station. This happened to me last Friday.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Brian87egotrip||09-26-2001||02:12 PM||||Mine started the I want gas cry, I made it to a gas station my wife spotted. I ran out as we pulled in, whew! Only to find out they were out of business.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> oh well! <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||09-26-2001||02:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>"Interesting side of empty?" LOL<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hehe...I thought that was pretty funny too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Nice "kill" stumpy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">           <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD(?)*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||09-26-2001||04:56 PM||||I have an issue with my 84.  As soon as it gets near the 1/4 mark, it will die whenever I take a Right hand turn.  It doesn't do it when I turn left, just right.  I usually take this as a sign to get gas.  The most I've been able to force into it has been 8.5 gallons when this happens.  Do I have another issue I should check??  This never happened on my 86 coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||09-26-2001||06:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jncomutt:<BR><B>I have an issue with my 84.  As soon as it gets near the 1/4 mark, it will die whenever I take a Right hand turn.  It doesn't do it when I turn left, just right.  I usually take this as a sign to get gas.  The most I've been able to force into it has been 8.5 gallons when this happens.  Do I have another issue I should check??  This never happened on my 86 coupe.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>HEE HEE...<BR>An 84 only holds 8 gallons, plus the .5 gal expansion/pipe capacity...<BR><P>------------------<BR>crash... The Fierowrecker<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/uploads/crash_sig.jpg">        <IMG SRC="http://fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||DKOV||09-26-2001||09:01 PM||||I found that my 88GT is OUT OF GAS when it reads 1/4 tank one day as I was sitting in the Drive through line at McD's.  What to do?<P>I was next door to a gas station, so I (I hope you're sitting down...)kept it in gear and used the STARTER to jolt myself out of line, into the street and into the gas station!!!<P>I guess you might call it my first attempt at an ELECTRIC Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyway, not good for the car OR the image!<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000009||banditbalz||09-26-2001||09:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Next time, silver Integra boy! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The funniest part of the whole thing is you still beat the Integra on a empty tank.... hahaha<BR>_<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/blackwhite2_1.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||09-27-2001||04:19 AM||||Fierowrecker--There were only two different tanks.  The '84-'86s had a 10.x gal tank and the '87s and '88s had an 11.x gal tank.  They didn't make an 8 gal tank as far as I know.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroRyan||09-27-2001||06:04 AM||||Yes they did, my 86 is an 8 gal.||||reg||1
Z||000012||SwissFormula||09-27-2001||07:59 AM||||Think positive:<BR>With no fuel your car is as light as it can be  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>My Formula does also run out of gas before it shows empty, i was lucky to pass a gas station when it happend to me.<BR>||||reg||7
