Z||000014||Cheever3000||09-27-2001||11:39 AM||||stimpy, I'm shocked!  Well, <I>somebody's</I> got to teach those Integra boyz a lesson, I don't know what lesson or why, but it needs to be taught.<P>The first thing an old autocross school told me was either race on full or on near empty, but they never mentioned "the interesting side of empty".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Both my 88GT and 88 Coupe are empty when the gauge says 1/4.  I have brought both of them to the pumps at a "dead stick".  Wouldn't want to try it again.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||LarryB||09-27-2001||11:51 AM||||The official capacities of the gas tanks are:<P>'84-'86 - 10.3 gallons<BR>'87-'88 - 11.9 gallons<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Brandon86SE||09-27-2001||02:38 PM||||Yes, that's true, or else 38L, and 45L for us Canadians.  However, the way the fuel pump is mounted in the tank, you'll never get to that last bit of gas.  I've ran my car dry and only got 35L into it.  Hope this clears some stuff up.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
